<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-chapter-title" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Fundamentals</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Welcome to the wonderful world of probable Pokémon!
    </p>

    <p>
      Throughout this course, we will explore the fundamentals and applications of
      calculus-based probability.  With the help of our Pokémon pals, we probably delve into
      the very-real applications of probability to Pokémon collecting and battles.  With an
      abstract lens, we will also have a firm foundation that will allow us to visualize how
      probability lies as a modeler of future events.
    </p>

    <p>
      This course will challenge and enhance both your computational and logical skills.
      You will be asking why.  You will be answering because.  You will showing that things
      always work or may not always work.  You will be connecting fundamentals of probability
      to algebra, calculus, discrete mathematics, and real analysis.  And, of course, you
      will be finding probabilities.
    </p>    
      
  </introduction>

